<hick:doc xmlns:hick="http://www.hickorydocs.com/1.0">

<hick:when test="iroh-relay">

## Iroh Relay Server

The Iroh relay server provides NAT traversal and peer discovery for Iroh-based
peer-to-peer applications. It acts as a STUN/TURN-like service that helps peers
behind NATs establish direct connections, falling back to relaying traffic when
direct connections aren't possible.

### Project Configuration

The Cargo.toml defines the relay server dependencies:

<hick:file path="iroh-relay/Cargo.toml">[package]
name = "<hick:val name="project_name" />-iroh-relay"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "<hick:val name="rust_edition" />"

[[bin]]
name = "<hick:val name="project_name" />-relay"
path = "src/main.rs"

[dependencies]
# Iroh relay server
iroh-relay = "0.31"
iroh-base = "0.31"

# Async runtime
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }

# Configuration and CLI
clap = { version = "4", features = ["derive", "env"] }
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
toml = "0.8"

# TLS
rcgen = "0.13"
rustls = "0.23"
rustls-pemfile = "2"

# Logging
tracing = "0.1"
tracing-subscriber = { version = "0.3", features = ["env-filter"] }

# Error handling
anyhow = "1"
thiserror = "2"

[dev-dependencies]
tempfile = "3"
</hick:file>

### Rust Toolchain

<hick:file path="iroh-relay/rust-toolchain.toml">[toolchain]
channel = "nightly"
</hick:file>

### Entry Point

The main binary parses configuration and starts the relay server:

<hick:file path="iroh-relay/src/main.rs">//! <hick:val name="project_name" /> Iroh Relay Server
//!
//! A relay server for NAT traversal and peer discovery in Iroh-based P2P networks.

mod config;
mod server;

use anyhow::Result;
use clap::Parser;
use tracing_subscriber::{layer::SubscriberExt, util::SubscriberInitExt};

#[derive(Parser)]
#[command(name = "<hick:val name="project_name" />-relay")]
#[command(about = "Iroh relay server for P2P networking")]
struct Cli {
    /// Path to configuration file
    #[arg(short, long, env = "RELAY_CONFIG")]
    config: Option<std::path::PathBuf>,

    /// HTTP bind address
    #[arg(long, env = "RELAY_HTTP_ADDR", default_value = "0.0.0.0:80")]
    http_addr: String,

    /// HTTPS bind address
    #[arg(long, env = "RELAY_HTTPS_ADDR", default_value = "0.0.0.0:443")]
    https_addr: String,

    /// QUIC bind address for native relay protocol
    #[arg(long, env = "RELAY_QUIC_ADDR", default_value = "0.0.0.0:3478")]
    quic_addr: String,

    /// Path to TLS certificate file (PEM format)
    #[arg(long, env = "RELAY_TLS_CERT")]
    tls_cert: Option<std::path::PathBuf>,

    /// Path to TLS private key file (PEM format)
    #[arg(long, env = "RELAY_TLS_KEY")]
    tls_key: Option<std::path::PathBuf>,

    /// Generate self-signed certificates (for development)
    #[arg(long, env = "RELAY_SELF_SIGNED", default_value = "false")]
    self_signed: bool,

    /// Hostname for the relay server (used in certificate generation)
    #[arg(long, env = "RELAY_HOSTNAME", default_value = "localhost")]
    hostname: String,
}

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<()> {
    // Initialize tracing
    tracing_subscriber::registry()
        .with(
            tracing_subscriber::EnvFilter::try_from_default_env()
                .unwrap_or_else(|_| "<hick:val name="project_name" />_iroh_relay=info,iroh_relay=info".into()),
        )
        .with(tracing_subscriber::fmt::layer())
        .init();

    let cli = Cli::parse();

    // Build configuration
    let config = if let Some(config_path) = cli.config {
        config::RelayConfig::from_file(&config_path)?
    } else {
        config::RelayConfig {
            http_addr: cli.http_addr.parse()?,
            https_addr: cli.https_addr.parse()?,
            quic_addr: cli.quic_addr.parse()?,
            tls_cert: cli.tls_cert,
            tls_key: cli.tls_key,
            self_signed: cli.self_signed,
            hostname: cli.hostname,
        }
    };

    tracing::info!("Starting <hick:val name="project_name" /> Iroh Relay Server");
    tracing::info!("HTTP: {}", config.http_addr);
    tracing::info!("HTTPS: {}", config.https_addr);
    tracing::info!("QUIC: {}", config.quic_addr);

    server::run(config).await
}
</hick:file>

### Configuration Module

<hick:file path="iroh-relay/src/config.rs">//! Configuration for the relay server

use anyhow::{Context, Result};
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use std::net::SocketAddr;
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};

/// Relay server configuration
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct RelayConfig {
    /// HTTP bind address (for health checks and HTTP->HTTPS redirect)
    #[serde(default = "default_http_addr")]
    pub http_addr: SocketAddr,

    /// HTTPS bind address
    #[serde(default = "default_https_addr")]
    pub https_addr: SocketAddr,

    /// QUIC bind address for native relay protocol
    #[serde(default = "default_quic_addr")]
    pub quic_addr: SocketAddr,

    /// Path to TLS certificate file
    pub tls_cert: Option<PathBuf>,

    /// Path to TLS private key file
    pub tls_key: Option<PathBuf>,

    /// Use self-signed certificates
    #[serde(default)]
    pub self_signed: bool,

    /// Hostname for certificate generation
    #[serde(default = "default_hostname")]
    pub hostname: String,
}

fn default_http_addr() -> SocketAddr {
    "0.0.0.0:80".parse().unwrap()
}

fn default_https_addr() -> SocketAddr {
    "0.0.0.0:443".parse().unwrap()
}

fn default_quic_addr() -> SocketAddr {
    "0.0.0.0:3478".parse().unwrap()
}

fn default_hostname() -> String {
    "localhost".to_string()
}

impl Default for RelayConfig {
    fn default() -> Self {
        Self {
            http_addr: default_http_addr(),
            https_addr: default_https_addr(),
            quic_addr: default_quic_addr(),
            tls_cert: None,
            tls_key: None,
            self_signed: true,
            hostname: default_hostname(),
        }
    }
}

impl RelayConfig {
    /// Load configuration from a TOML file
    pub fn from_file(path: &Path) -> Result<Self> {
        let content = std::fs::read_to_string(path)
            .with_context(|| format!("Failed to read config file: {}", path.display()))?;
        let config: RelayConfig = toml::from_str(&content)
            .with_context(|| format!("Failed to parse config file: {}", path.display()))?;
        Ok(config)
    }
}
</hick:file>

### Server Module

<hick:file path="iroh-relay/src/server.rs">//! Relay server implementation

use anyhow::{Context, Result};
use iroh_relay::server::{
    AccessConfig, CertConfig, QuicConfig, RelayConfig as IrohRelayConfig,
    Server, ServerConfig, TlsConfig,
};
use std::sync::Arc;

use crate::config::RelayConfig;

/// Run the relay server
pub async fn run(config: RelayConfig) -> Result<()> {
    let (tls_config, server_config) = create_tls_config(&config)?;

    let quic_config = QuicConfig {
        server_config: server_config.clone(),
        bind_addr: config.quic_addr,
    };

    let relay_config = IrohRelayConfig {
        http_bind_addr: config.http_addr,
        tls: Some(tls_config),
        limits: Default::default(),
        key_cache_capacity: Some(10_000),
        access: AccessConfig::Everyone,
    };

    let server_config = ServerConfig {
        relay: Some(relay_config),
        quic: Some(quic_config),
        ..Default::default()
    };

    tracing::info!("Spawning relay server...");
    let server = Server::spawn(server_config)
        .await
        .context("Failed to spawn relay server")?;

    if let Some(https_addr) = server.https_addr() {
        tracing::info!("Relay server listening on https://{}", https_addr);
    }
    if let Some(quic_addr) = server.quic_addr() {
        tracing::info!("QUIC relay listening on {}", quic_addr);
    }

    // Keep the server running
    tracing::info!("Relay server is ready");
    tokio::signal::ctrl_c().await?;
    tracing::info!("Shutting down...");

    Ok(())
}

/// Create TLS configuration from the relay config
fn create_tls_config(config: &RelayConfig) -> Result<(TlsConfig, Arc<rustls::ServerConfig>)> {
    let (certs, key, server_config) = if config.self_signed {
        tracing::info!("Generating self-signed certificate for {}", config.hostname);
        generate_self_signed_cert(&config.hostname)?
    } else {
        let cert_path = config.tls_cert.as_ref()
            .context("TLS certificate path required when not using self-signed")?;
        let key_path = config.tls_key.as_ref()
            .context("TLS key path required when not using self-signed")?;

        tracing::info!("Loading TLS certificate from {}", cert_path.display());
        load_tls_files(cert_path, key_path)?
    };

    let tls_config = TlsConfig {
        cert: CertConfig::<(), ()>::Manual { certs },
        https_bind_addr: config.https_addr,
        quic_bind_addr: config.quic_addr,
        server_config: server_config.clone(),
    };

    Ok((tls_config, server_config))
}

/// Generate a self-signed certificate for development
fn generate_self_signed_cert(
    hostname: &str,
) -> Result<(Vec<rustls::pki_types::CertificateDer<'static>>, rustls::pki_types::PrivateKeyDer<'static>, Arc<rustls::ServerConfig>)> {
    use rcgen::{CertifiedKey, generate_simple_self_signed};

    let subject_alt_names = vec![
        hostname.to_string(),
        "localhost".to_string(),
        "127.0.0.1".to_string(),
    ];

    let CertifiedKey { cert, key_pair } = generate_simple_self_signed(subject_alt_names)
        .context("Failed to generate self-signed certificate")?;

    let cert_der = cert.der().clone();
    let key_der = key_pair.serialize_der();

    let certs = vec![cert_der];
    let key = rustls::pki_types::PrivateKeyDer::Pkcs8(key_der.into());

    let server_config = rustls::ServerConfig::builder()
        .with_no_client_auth()
        .with_single_cert(certs.clone(), key.clone_key())
        .context("Failed to create rustls server config")?;

    Ok((certs, key, Arc::new(server_config)))
}

/// Load TLS certificate and key from files
fn load_tls_files(
    cert_path: &std::path::Path,
    key_path: &std::path::Path,
) -> Result<(Vec<rustls::pki_types::CertificateDer<'static>>, rustls::pki_types::PrivateKeyDer<'static>, Arc<rustls::ServerConfig>)> {
    use std::io::BufReader;

    let cert_file = std::fs::File::open(cert_path)
        .with_context(|| format!("Failed to open certificate file: {}", cert_path.display()))?;
    let mut cert_reader = BufReader::new(cert_file);
    let certs: Vec<_> = rustls_pemfile::certs(&mut cert_reader)
        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()
        .context("Failed to parse certificate file")?;

    let key_file = std::fs::File::open(key_path)
        .with_context(|| format!("Failed to open key file: {}", key_path.display()))?;
    let mut key_reader = BufReader::new(key_file);
    let key = rustls_pemfile::private_key(&mut key_reader)
        .context("Failed to parse key file")?
        .context("No private key found in key file")?;

    let server_config = rustls::ServerConfig::builder()
        .with_no_client_auth()
        .with_single_cert(certs.clone(), key.clone_key())
        .context("Failed to create rustls server config")?;

    Ok((certs, key, Arc::new(server_config)))
}
</hick:file>

### Dockerfile

The Dockerfile builds a minimal container for the relay server:

<hick:file path="iroh-relay/Dockerfile"># syntax=docker/dockerfile:1

# Build stage
FROM rust:1.83-slim-bookworm AS builder

WORKDIR /app

# Install build dependencies
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    pkg-config \
    libssl-dev \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# Copy manifests
COPY Cargo.toml Cargo.lock* ./

# Create dummy source to cache dependencies
RUN mkdir src && echo "fn main() {}" > src/main.rs

# Build dependencies (this layer is cached)
RUN cargo build --release && rm -rf src

# Copy actual source
COPY src ./src

# Build the actual binary
RUN touch src/main.rs && cargo build --release

# Runtime stage
FROM debian:bookworm-slim

WORKDIR /app

# Install runtime dependencies
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    ca-certificates \
    curl \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# Copy binary from builder
COPY --from=builder /app/target/release/<hick:val name="project_name" />-relay /usr/local/bin/relay

# Create non-root user
RUN useradd -r -s /bin/false relay
USER relay

# Expose ports
# HTTP (health checks, redirect)
EXPOSE 80
# HTTPS (WebSocket relay)
EXPOSE 443
# QUIC (native relay protocol)
EXPOSE 3478/udp

# Health check
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s --start-period=5s --retries=3 \
    CMD curl -f http://localhost:80/health || exit 1

# Default environment
ENV RELAY_HTTP_ADDR=0.0.0.0:80
ENV RELAY_HTTPS_ADDR=0.0.0.0:443
ENV RELAY_QUIC_ADDR=0.0.0.0:3478
ENV RELAY_SELF_SIGNED=true
ENV RELAY_HOSTNAME=localhost
ENV RUST_LOG=info

ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/relay"]
</hick:file>

### Docker Compose

For local development with the relay server:

<hick:file path="iroh-relay/docker-compose.yml">services:
  relay:
    build: .
    ports:
      - "8080:80"      # HTTP
      - "8443:443"     # HTTPS
      - "3478:3478/udp" # QUIC
    environment:
      - RELAY_SELF_SIGNED=true
      - RELAY_HOSTNAME=localhost
      - RUST_LOG=info,iroh_relay=debug
    restart: unless-stopped
</hick:file>

### Example Configuration File

<hick:file path="iroh-relay/config.example.toml"># <hick:val name="project_name" /> Iroh Relay Server Configuration

# HTTP bind address (for health checks and redirects)
http_addr = "0.0.0.0:80"

# HTTPS bind address (for WebSocket relay)
https_addr = "0.0.0.0:443"

# QUIC bind address (for native relay protocol)
quic_addr = "0.0.0.0:3478"

# TLS Configuration
# For production, provide certificate and key files:
# tls_cert = "/etc/ssl/certs/relay.crt"
# tls_key = "/etc/ssl/private/relay.key"

# For development, use self-signed certificates:
self_signed = true
hostname = "localhost"
</hick:file>

